  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Clear skies and drier conditions will \ncontinue to cool temperatures tonight. Low temperatures tonight \nwill remain around 5 degrees below normal with lows hovering \naround the low 20s. An upper level ridge will continue to build \nover our area bringing with it mostly sunny skies, drier \nconditions, and above normal temperatures. Highs for the rest of \nthe week will remain in the upper 60s, with some areas peaking in \nthe low 70s this weekend. \n\nLooking ahead in to next week, a polar jet will be making its way\nin to our region, bringing with it the chance for winter weather\nand colder temperatures. A cold front associated with an upper\nlevel trough will reduce our highs back to the 40s and 50s, as\nwell as bring with it the chances for precipitation on Monday into\nTuesday. These cooler temperatures will also bring our lows down\ninto the 20s and 30s next week. While these lows bring us the\nslightest bit of hope at building the first snowman of the season,\nconfidence in the timing and intensity of this forecast is still\nlow as it is still beyond the forecast period. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence is in the\nforecast for the remainder of the week. Moderate confidence is in\nthe forecast for the cooling temperatures early next week. Low\nconfidence remains in the timing and intensity of the front and\nits associated precipitation chances early next week. No\ndeviations from the NBM at this time.",
